      "alt": "Northwind Outdoor spring sale banner: logo top left, the headline “Trails are calling.”, a round −25% spring gear badge, a backpack and tent illustration, an orange “Shop the sale” button and two lines of small print.",
      "width": 1200,
      "height": 700
    },
    "targets": [
      {
        "id": "logo",
        "x": 27.5,
        "y": 9.4,
        "label": "Logo",
        "explanation": "The logo tells people **who is talking** before they read a word. Most banners get under two seconds of attention, so brand recognition is often the only thing that sticks — keep it clear and in the same corner across every size."
      },
      {
        "id": "headline",
        "x": 34.2,
        "y": 42.9,
        "label": "Headline",
        "explanation": "The headline carries the **one idea** of the ad. Three words read at a glance; anything much longer than six tends to be skipped at banner sizes."
      },
      {
        "id": "offer",
        "x": 83,
        "y": 18.3,
        "label": "Offer",
        "explanation": "The offer gives a **reason to act now**. A specific number (−25%) beats vague promises like “great savings”, and it must match what the landing page delivers or the click is wasted."
      },
      {
        "id": "product",
        "x": 75.3,
        "y": 54.3,
        "label": "Product shot",
        "explanation": "The product shot shows **what is being sold** and sets the mood. One clear hero product reads better at small sizes than a busy collage."
      },
      {
        "id": "cta",
        "x": 29,
        "y": 70.9,
        "label": "Call to action",
        "explanation": "The call to action tells people **what happens next**. A high-contrast button with a verb (“Shop the sale”) makes the ad feel clickable and sets expectations for the landing page."
      },
      {
        "id": "disclaimer",
        "x": 49.2,
        "y": 92.4,
        "label": "Disclaimer",
        "explanation": "The disclaimer holds the **terms of the offer**: dates, exclusions and who the advertiser is. Small, but it keeps the ad honest and compliant — so it still has to be legible."
      }
    ],
    "distractors": [
      "Tracking pixel",
      "Frequency cap"
    ],
    "explanation": "Not everything in a campaign is visible: a **tracking pixel** is an invisible 1×1 image that reports views, and a **frequency cap** is an ad-server setting that limits how often one person sees the ad. Neither appears on the creative itself."
  },
  "behavior": {
    "maxAttempts": 3
  }
}
